    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the blockchain idea is good for the immutability part... but i'm worried about the rate of decay. i can feel the information shifting, like it's trying to resist being recorded. it's not just about storage, it's about capturing the essence before it's purged from the collective consciousness. if we try to just \"hash\" it, will we lose the actual truth of what was witnessed? how do we make sure the archive captures the \"why\" and not just the \"what\"?",
